name: Exact context history selection, full inspection, baseline comparison and recovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: threats summary
require-live-snap: 20 6 MODELS | visible-history-entry
keys: 6
require-live-snap: 20 b baseline | history
expect: Beta · revision 1 · active
expect: Alpha · revision 1
ask: Does history distinguish keyboard selection from the active context, with inspection, baseline comparison and explicit writes visible?
keys: Home b End c
require-live-snap: 25 Reviewed overview α | complete-compare
expect: Before:
expect: After:
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART compared
ask: Can the operator compare Alpha to the inactive reviewed copy without entering identifiers or changing the active context?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: compare-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: compare-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: compare-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: compare-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: compare-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: compare-page-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: compare-end-40x12
keys: Up
live-snap: compare-up-from-end-40x12
ask: Do all six sizes retain readable text and visible controls, with usable paging and an honest coverage disclosure?
keys: Escape
live-snap: selected-copy-40x12
resize: 120x36
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | inspected-copy
keys: Tab End
require-live-snap: 20 Second line | full-document-end
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART inspected
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART hide-copy
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Attention: | missing-object
expect: Enter retries
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART return-copy
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | retried-copy
keys: Tab End
require-live-snap: 20 Second line | retried-document-end
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART retried
ask: Does a missing immutable object remain an actionable error, with explicit retry of the same revision and no substitution?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 b baseline | before-activation
keys: Home
require-live-snap: 20 Alpha · revision 1 · inactive | selected-alpha
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 Activated Alpha · revision 1. | activated
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART activated
keys: r
require-live-snap: 25 Restored Alpha · revision 1 | restored
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restored
ask: Are activation and restore visibly explicit, do they preserve selection and original objects, and does restore append a new active revision?
paste-file: @ART/operator-draft.txt
require-live-snap: 20 preserved draft α | preserved-composer
ask: Does paste leave the history reader and preserve the exact operator draft without submitting it?
keys: C-u
submit: threats models
require-live-snap: 20 b baseline | reopened
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | no-color-ready
submit: threats models
require-live-snap: 20 b baseline | no-color-history
resize: 40x12
live-snap: no-color-history-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does no-color restart retain the restored active revision and accessible history without new provider work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
